WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.920
From Jurassic Park and Jumanji to Kong: Skull&nbsp;
Island and Journey to the Center of the Earth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.920
it’s safe to say that humans have long&nbsp;
imagined what it might be like to visit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:15.280
the prehistoric eras of this planet’s history.&nbsp;
Perhaps it comes from knowing that the Earth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:20.960
was once so dramatically different back before we&nbsp;
evolved into the dominant species on the planet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:26.160
Then again, maybe the fantasy of traveling&nbsp;
back to a land that time forgot is simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.880
in the appeal of how cool it would be&nbsp;
to see an actual dinosaur up close.&nbsp;

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.560
Regardless of the reasoning,&nbsp;
without access to a time machine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:40.480
you would find it difficult to make your way&nbsp;
back to any era of the primeval world. Unless, of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:48.480
course, you happened to accidentally stumble upon&nbsp;
SCP-1265, also known as the Mesozoic Preserve.&nbsp;

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:54.320
This anomalous location is an irregular landmass&nbsp;
found within the basin of the Congo River,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:59.680
in Central Africa. The oddly shaped portion&nbsp;
of land, measuring fifty kilometers cubed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.000
is mostly contained within the Democratic&nbsp;
Republic of the Congo. However, around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.840
fifteen of those cubed kilometers spill over into&nbsp;
what is known as just the Republic of the Congo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:17.120
the neighboring smaller country of the two that&nbsp;
the Congo is split into. SCP-1265 appears, at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:23.360
first, to be a very unremarkable area, populated&nbsp;
only by a sparse number of tribal villages.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:28.560
The place is mostly uninhabited, and, in fact,&nbsp;
there is very little unusual about the local&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.080
flora and fauna that marks it as being any&nbsp;
different from the surrounding Congo basin.&nbsp;

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.080
That is, unless you count&nbsp;
the dinosaurs, of course.&nbsp;

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:45.120
SCP-1265 is, as its alternate name might suggest,&nbsp;
home to a number of remarkable species that are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:50.320
thought to have been extinct for many hundreds&nbsp;
of millions of years. While they cannot be seen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:55.120
all roaming around the area like the famous&nbsp;
moment from the first Jurassic Park movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.120 --> 00:02:00.000
once every thirty days, these creatures will&nbsp;
appear in a group of approximately five.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.280
Collectively designated as SCP-1265-A, these&nbsp;
dinosaurs are not necessarily those known to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:12.800
have their fossils found within Africa itself, but&nbsp;
appear to be mostly heralding from the Mesozoic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:18.480
Era, and only those that evolved in similar&nbsp;
climates to those found in the Congo Basin.&nbsp;

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.440
Now, while you might expect some of the big names&nbsp;
to come rampaging through the jungle, we’re afraid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:28.080
we might have to burst your bubble. You will not&nbsp;
find the likes of the famous Tyrannosaurus Rex&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:34.800
or the Brachiosaurus in SCP-1265. As a matter&nbsp;
of fact, it’s actually highly rare to find any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:40.240
species there that have been previously uncovered&nbsp;
in North America according to the fossil records.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:43.920
The most relatively common American&nbsp;
dinosaur species to appear as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:50.640
instances of SCP-1265-A are the Spinosaurus&nbsp;
and Kentrosaurus. So you’re in luck if your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:58.080
favorite Jurassic Park movie was Jurassic Park 3.
SCP-1265-A dinos aren’t all from the same period&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:02.560
of the Mesozoic either, but the most common&nbsp;
prehistoric eras represented in the Preserve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:08.400
are the Cretaceous and Jurassic. There have even&nbsp;
been a few Triassic era dinosaurs spotted there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.520
as well as several non-dinosaur reptiles.&nbsp;
Pterosaurs and similar creatures are known to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:20.800
exist within SCP-1265 but are not commonly seen.
There are, perhaps highly surprisingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:26.640
a number of dinosaurs that appear as&nbsp;
instances of SCP-1265-A that do not match&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:31.280
any known to be discovered on the fossil&nbsp;
record. These new creatures are known under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:39.200
the collective designation of SCP-1265-a
instead of the upper case ‘A’.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:46.160
The SCP-1265-a creatures are known to&nbsp;
be unusually aggressive, especially when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:50.320
compared to their other counterparts that&nbsp;
have been encountered within the Preserve.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:56.640
Most of the time, even carnivorous species that&nbsp;
appear in SCP-1265 are normally pretty docile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:01.600
and show no notable fear or aggression&nbsp;
towards humans unless they are provoked.&nbsp;

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:08.960
SCP-1265-a, however, tends to be the biggest&nbsp;
exception to that rule. These unknown, unrecorded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:14.320
dinosaurs will often charge directly at any&nbsp;
Foundation researchers on-site when they arrive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.400
and will even indiscriminately attack&nbsp;
and viscously slaughter other animals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:23.680
around the Preserve. For a time, the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation was unable to determine the exact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:29.475
origins of these previously uncategorized&nbsp;
dinosaur species that make up SCP-1265-a,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:36.800
that is, until some were found within the&nbsp;
fossil record. These creatures that became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:42.160
identified and recorded through the discovery of&nbsp;
similar or matching fossils soon ceased behaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:51.200
with active hostility towards humans in SCP-1265.
Any and all instances of SCP-1265-A are incapable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:56.080
of leaving the surrounding area that forms&nbsp;
the Mesozoic Preserve. Every time that one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:02.640
of the dinosaurs attempts to cross the border that&nbsp;
surrounds SCP-1265, the creature will vanish from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:10.080
sight, completely dematerializing in the blink&nbsp;
of an eye. The SCP-1265-A instance will reappear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:14.880
shortly after, within three kilometers from&nbsp;
the border. On discovery, the dinosaurs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:22.160
appear heavily sedated, but still alive.
The existence of SCP-1265 dates back so far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:27.040
that it even crops up in local folklore.&nbsp;
According to historical records and various&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:32.400
reports of numerous dinosaur sightings over the&nbsp;
years, the Mesozoic Preserve is believed to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:38.720
existed for almost two hundred years. The SCP&nbsp;
Foundation conducted interviews with members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:43.920
of local tribes, most notably a resident&nbsp;
belonging to a nearby M’boshi village,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:48.960
who shed more light on the role some of the&nbsp;
dinosaurs have had on their tribe’s livelihood.&nbsp;

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:54.640
One tribesperson noted that, while many of the&nbsp;
creatures didn’t eat people, there were occasional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.640 --> 00:06:02.640
exceptions. One instance of SCP-1265-A that did&nbsp;
appear carnivorous was known as ‘Nguma-monene’,&nbsp;

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:08.640
and was described as resembling a large snake that&nbsp;
walked on all fours like a dog, with a big ridge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:14.720
over its back. This is most likely referring to&nbsp;
either a specific Spinosaurus or the species as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:19.040
a whole. Then, there was the dinosaur that&nbsp;
the local people called ‘Mokele-mbembe’,&nbsp;

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:26.160
the largest of all the SCP-1265-A&nbsp;
instances. This was apparently an aquatic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:30.480
or semi-aquatic dinosaur, capable of&nbsp;
breathing underwater and large enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:36.320
to cause tremors in the ground whenever it walked.
Mokele was most likely a word for the Camarasaurus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:42.560
species. There was also Mbielu-Mbielu-Mbielu,
sometimes called ‘the beast with planks in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:47.840
its back’ by the locals, referring&nbsp;
to the Kentrosaurus in SCP-1265.&nbsp;

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:53.520
According to further testimony from the local&nbsp;
tribespeople, the Mbielu and Mokele both possessed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:58.240
features not present in most modern&nbsp;
illustrations that depict such dinosaurs;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:03.440
namely, almost all of them possessed feathers.
“They are almost like birds in that way,” the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:09.440
tribesperson explained, “But they do not&nbsp;
fly. The ones that do fly have no feathers.”&nbsp;

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:12.400
While that might not sound as though&nbsp;
it’s in keeping with the scaly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:17.600
reptilian nature of most depictions of&nbsp;
dinosaurs, there’s actually some sense to this.&nbsp;

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:22.800
You see, dinosaurs are mostly theropods, a&nbsp;
subcategory of creatures that evolved into certain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:30.160
animals still alive today: but we call them birds&nbsp;
nowadays. In the 1990s, at the Yixian Formation in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:35.760
Liaoning, China, paleontologists uncovered the&nbsp;
first fossil evidence of feathered dinosaurs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.760
with the bones of a Sinosauropteryx&nbsp;
being the earliest fossils to bear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:45.760
imprinting that suggested dinosaurs had feathers.
The same local tribesperson also believed the area&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:51.840
of the Congo basin containing SCP-1265 was&nbsp;
hexed, given how none of the dinosaurs could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:57.280
leave without vanishing spontaneously. The same&nbsp;
happened whenever one tried to take their meat or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:02.720
their eggs from the Preserve. Apparently, a number&nbsp;
of years before, a gang of hunters had managed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:07.600
kill a Camarasaurus and attempted to take the&nbsp;
creature’s carcass from the area. The hunters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:12.480
were forced to enlist the help of local villagers,&nbsp;
and it took the combined strength of all of them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:18.000
to move it to the very edge of the Preserve.
Of course, you can guess what happened next:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:23.680
the creature disappeared, leaving the hunters&nbsp;
unable to claim their prize. Over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:30.000
the locals have witnessed countless others&nbsp;
try to visit SCP-1265, but not to hunt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:35.360
just to catch a glimpse of a wandering dinosaur,&nbsp;
despite how dangerous that endeavor is.&nbsp;

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:41.440
The Foundation conducts monthly expeditions&nbsp;
through SCP-1265, studying any changes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:46.560
the wildlife and often harvesting any dinosaur&nbsp;
eggs they come across. After incubating them for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:52.000
a time, the Foundation’s researchers will study&nbsp;
the newborn dinosaurs until they reach maturity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:56.480
at which point they are then released back&nbsp;
into the wild within the Mesozoic Preserve.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.480 --> 00:09:01.440
Naturally, this all occurs on location&nbsp;
at Site 1265, which is maintained as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:06.880
wildlife preserve under the false organization&nbsp;
name the ‘Safe and Clean Planet Initiative’.&nbsp;

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:11.760
During one of these monthly expeditions, one&nbsp;
Doctor Neill, a Foundation researcher, made a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:17.360
series of notes regarding the prehistoric wildlife&nbsp;
contained within the Preserve. According to Neill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:22.080
there are a number of trilobites that dwell&nbsp;
in the water. These are ancient arthropods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:26.880
armored precursors to modern insects&nbsp;
and shellfish; basically, picture a big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:33.200
underwater woodlouse. Apparently, the locals&nbsp;
would fish for trilobites within SCP-1265,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:39.680
and they taste like prawns when cooked and eaten.
While exploring SCP-1265, Doctor Neill discovered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:45.440
a family of Baryonyx, a large dinosaur with&nbsp;
a long jaw similar to that of a crocodile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:51.200
that mostly fed on fish. Neill observed as&nbsp;
these Baryonyx approached a clan of Spinosaurus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:56.640
that according to him, looked more like ducks than&nbsp;
anything else thanks to their coating of feathers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.640 --> 00:10:01.360
The researcher mourned a profound disappointment&nbsp;
that he and another doctor, Doctor Moore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:07.280
had felt in seeing the Spinosaurus up close.
“Their skeletal structure is completely unsuited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:13.520
for walking upright, and the less said about&nbsp;
the so-called spine, the better. Scientifically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:19.280
fascinating, but as a life-long dinosaur&nbsp;
enthusiast, I must grieve for such a titan.”&nbsp;

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:24.560
Later in the expedition, Doctor Neill discovered&nbsp;
the first of a completely new species of dinosaur,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:33.280
a new SCP-1265-a instance. The creature was&nbsp;
iridescent black, similar in color to a raven,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:39.840
and possessed four wings, one on each arm&nbsp;
and one on each leg. There was speculation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:46.160
among the expedition team that this was a brand&nbsp;
new, never before seen species of Microraptor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:54.560
possibly native to the continent of Asia during a&nbsp;
prehistoric time period. Being an SCP-1265-a, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.560 --> 00:11:00.000
creature was noticeably aggressive, but the team&nbsp;
was able to capture and sedate it, temporarily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.960
naming it the ‘Microraptor foundationii’.
Next, Neill and the rest of the team witnessed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:11.200
a Postosuchus, a species of crocodile from the&nbsp;
late Triassic era, drinking at the edge of a lake.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:16.320
The prehistoric croc was suddenly attacked by a&nbsp;
pack of Coelophysis, which were small carnivores&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:21.680
that used their size and speed to take down&nbsp;
large prey as a group. They ate the Postosuchus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:26.880
stripping it right down to the bone like a school&nbsp;
of piranha ripping apart a cow in the Amazon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:32.800
The intrepid expedition party then witnessed a&nbsp;
fight between a Therizinosaurus and a Carnotaurus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:37.280
wherein the victorious Therizinosaurus&nbsp;
dipped its claws in the blood of its fallen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:42.880
enemy and used it to mark its territory,&nbsp;
scoring trees with Carnotaurus blood.&nbsp;

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:51.040
Finally, the group discovered yet another new&nbsp;
SCP-1265-a instance, this time a ceratopsidae.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:55.280
These were a sub-group of dinosaurs&nbsp;
that were mainly four-legged herbivores,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.280 --> 00:12:01.040
including the likes of the famous Triceratops.&nbsp;
This new ceratopsidae, much like many others in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:07.360
the fossil record, possessed four short, stumpy&nbsp;
legs but only one singular horn for defense. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:12.640
the Foundation expedition encountered it, it had&nbsp;
been engaged in combat with a Pachyrhinosaurus;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:18.160
a horned ceratopsidae highly similar to the&nbsp;
Triceratops, but usually with a row of horns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:23.520
or horns protruding from its frill, as&nbsp;
opposed to the Triceratops’ trio of horns.&nbsp;

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:31.360
Unlike other members of the ceratopsidae family,&nbsp;
this new SCP-1265-a instance did not have the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:36.800
characteristic frill, instead appeared to have&nbsp;
a pair of floppy ears at the top of its head.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:45.280
The newly discovered dinosaur was also, like the&nbsp;
other SCP-1265-a instances, a lot more aggressive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:50.880
and gored the Pachyrhinosaurus with its horn.
At this current moment in time, it is unknown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:58.320
exactly how the dinosaurs in the Congo basin&nbsp;
actually came to be in SCP-1265. The fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:02.080
they cannot leave its borders suggests that&nbsp;
they were placed there with the intention of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:07.520
being confined to that area, but there is no way&nbsp;
of knowing if these dinosaurs were lifted out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:12.720
their rightful place in time to the modern-day.&nbsp;
It could be that they survived for millions of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:18.080
years without evolving, or have perhaps traveled&nbsp;
to our time from their prehistoric eras through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:24.240
some form of temporal gateway, a door through&nbsp;
time. Unless, of course, somebody spared no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:30.160
expense and grew these dinosaurs from scratch,&nbsp;
but who’d be mad enough to try that, right?&nbsp;

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:35.760
Now go check out “You Can't Resist SCP-666&nbsp;
- Spirit Lodge” and “You'll NEVER Make It To&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:41.920
SCP-084 - Static Tower” for more locations&nbsp;
it’s dangerous to even set foot in!

